{"skill":{"slug":"markdown-converter","displayName":"Markdown Converter"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767651965151,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1968,"sha256":"354b8335051b9037e8c23324c33f68b3abbdac5ab9cfa12935c26b53575cf488","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1744,"sha256":"5dac645aa048fb5d521fca32c763d03b93a0821cf5fbc06b772bc4c127f988b1","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789014993546,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"9caa8c989b8fff4ce32ef8c8f8f45ec42224744a4f1766bfc35f0b2dd296508b","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/9caa8c989b8fff4ce32ef8c8f8f45ec42224744a4f1766bfc35f0b2dd296508b","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: markdown-converter\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. It provides instructions for converting various file types to Markdown using the `uvx markitdown` utility. All commands and options described in `SKILL.md` are directly related to this stated purpose, including local file operations and an optional integration with Azure Document Intelligence for enhanced PDF extraction. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts against the AI agent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159639405},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789014993546},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward Markdown conversion helper, but users should understand that it runs a third-party command through uvx at runtime.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The requested access is proportionate for document conversion, but conversion tools may read supplied files, process URLs, use optional Azure Document Intelligence, and access the invoking process environment like any local command.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill relies on `uvx markitdown`, which can download, cache, and execute the current package and dependencies without a pinned version.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Commands are user-directed examples for converting specified input files or stdin to Markdown output; no hidden role changes, prompt overrides, broad indexing, or unrelated actions were found.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No backdoor, service, scheduled task, privilege escalation, or persistent agent behavior was found; the only persistence noted is normal uvx dependency caching.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is converting documents and media to Markdown, and the instructions consistently invoke markitdown for that purpose only.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable letting Codex run `uvx markitdown` on files you choose. For sensitive documents, prefer a pinned/reviewed markitdown version or a sandboxed environment with limited file, credential, and network access.","findings":"[T08] expected: The unpinned `uvx markitdown` invocation is a real supply-chain consideration, but it is directly tied to the skill's conversion purpose and the artifact contains no evidence of malicious or deceptive package use.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789014993546}}}}}